Unchanged from the sweep-fix plan: Fulfil 'ship' decrements processed tracked stock once, under the routing claim, in its transaction (F-26). Spec inlined from the wave-11b packet file (scoped at fb00af1c; fixture prefix v99c_): This packet was scoped at fb00af1c. Wave 11a (29 packets, owner rulings D-116..D-139) has landed since, on the base you build from: read the current code and `git log --oneline fb00af1c..HEAD -- <file>` for every file in your write set before you start. Where wave 11a already changed what the packet describes, build on it; where the packet premise no longer holds, report a CONTRADICTION deviation and do the smallest change that meets the packet intent. Owner ruling D-136 applies (no cancel after shipping). Write a SHIP StockMovement audit row (type SALE or SHIP as the existing vocabulary allows, reason SHIP, the acting member) for each processed tracked line it decrements, if the existing StockMovement vocabulary has a fitting type; else record why not. DEFECT (F-26). fulfillOrder 'process' (apps/server/src/modules/marketplace/marketplace.service.ts:1674-1683) calls createPickPackTasks (apps/server/src/modules/marketplace/fulfillment-routing.service.ts:1421-1481), which moves RESERVED, PO_RAISED, PREORDER_ACCEPTED and AWAITING_MANUAL routes to PICKING_PACKING. fulfillOrder 'ship' (marketplace.service.ts:1685-1749) decrements stock only for LOCAL_STOCK routes still RESERVED (:1717-1729), then moves PICKING_PACKING routes to SHIPPED with no stock write (:1731-1746). 'ship' is only allowed from picking_packing (VALID_ORDER_TRANSITIONS, fulfillment-routing.service.ts:219-232: routed → picking_packing → shipped). So on the normal route → process → ship flow, tracked stock is never decremented and its reservation never released.

REPRODUCED at fb00af1c on a real DB: an order created paid with tracked A×2 was routed (A at 10 on hand / 2 reserved), processed and shipped. The route became SHIPPED and A stayed at 10/2.

Two further defects. decrementInventoryOnShip (fulfillment-routing.service.ts:989-1028) reads the stock row and writes absolute quantity and reserved values outside any transaction and lock. That is a lost update against routing, which locks the row and writes reserved = locked value + q. And every 'ship' write (shipment, routes, stock) happens before, and outside, the transaction that writes the shipped status (:1865-1873). So two concurrent ships both pass canTransitionOrder on the status read at :1563 and both decrement.

FIX:
(1) Do all of 'ship''s writes in the final transaction (ROUTING_CLAIM_TX_OPTIONS), in this order:
  - claimOrderRouting(tx, businessId, orderId);
  - re-read the order's status and items under the claim and refuse with 400 unless canTransitionOrder(status,'shipped');
  - create the Shipment (when carrier or trackingNumber is given);
  - read the order's LOCAL_STOCK routes in RESERVED or PICKING_PACKING;
  - lock the (productId of the route's item, warehouseId) stock rows of the tracked ones with lockStockRowPairsInOrder (apps/server/src/core/inventory/stock-lock-order.ts), skipping routes that are noReservationRequired, untracked or virtual, or have no warehouseId;
  - for each route, run a compare-and-set updateMany({id, status in [RESERVED, PICKING_PACKING]}) to SHIPPED with shipmentId. Only when count === 1 and the route is tracked, read the stock row under the lock and write quantity = max(0, quantity − q) and reserved = max(0, reserved − q), keeping today's clamps;
  - then the existing updateMany moving PICKING_PACKING, PO_RAISED and PREORDER_ACCEPTED routes to SHIPPED;
  - then the timeline step and the order status, as today.
  After commit: checkAndAlertReorderThreshold for each decremented row, then the lifecycle event and the notification, unchanged.
(2) Replace decrementInventoryOnShip(businessId, routeId) with a helper that takes tx, used only from the ship transaction (its only caller is marketplace.service.ts:1721). Update the writer list in stock-lock-order.ts's header comment: the ship decrement now locks its pairs first.

MUST NOT CHANGE: the transition table; 'process' behaviour; MANUAL, DROPSHIP and PREORDER routes still go to SHIPPED; untracked and virtual lines write no stock; one event and one notification per ship; RC-01..RC-23.

OUT OF SCOPE: PATCH .../status 'shipped', a label write that moves no stock (new residual, needs a ruling on whether PATCH should run the ship path, which would refuse the web dropdown's routed → SHIPPED); StockMovement audit rows for ship decrements (none are written today). Sweep-fix plan detail (inlined): (wave-11b spec inlined in this packet.) The wave-11b prefix v99c_ is superseded: SWEEP-P0 has since registered v99c_/v99f_/v99i_/v99j_/v99k_/v99w_, and x01*_ heads fail the registry's NEW_PREFIX rule (k<NN><a-z>_ or v<NN><a-z>_). A suite this packet extends keeps that suite's own prefix; a new suite takes the prefix allocated above.
